agraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ%Say not thou, I will recompense evil;¦layout ‚¤textÙ-But wait on the LORD, and he shall save thee.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses˜„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines’‚¤textÙ0Divers weights are an abomination unto the LORD;¦layout ‚¤textÙ And a false balance is not good.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤text½Man's goings are of the LORD;¦layout ‚¤textÙ*How can a man then understand his own way?¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ:It is a snare to the man who devoureth that which is holy,¦layout ‚¤text¿And after vows to make enquiry.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ"A wise king scattereth the wicked,¦layout ‚¤textÙ!And bringeth the wheel over them.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ,The spirit of man is the candle of the LORD,¦layout ‚¤textÙ,Searching all the inward parts of the belly.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ"Mercy and truth preserve the king:¦layout ‚¤textÙ$And his throne is upholden by mercy.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ)The glory of young men is their strength:¦layout ‚¤textÙ+And the beauty of old men is the grey head.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ,The blueness of a wound cleanseth away evil:¦layout ‚¤textÙ,So do stripes the inward parts of the belly.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse